-- Basic parsing
RFC 7617: user=[Aladdin] password=[open sesame]
lowercase scheme: user=[Aladdin] password=[open sesame]
two spaces: user=[Aladdin] password=[open sesame]
colon in the password: user=[ada] password=[pa:ss:word]
empty password: user=[ada] password=[]
empty user: user=[] password=[pw]
UTF-8: user=[José] password=[pässwörd 🔑]
RFC 7617 test:123: user=[test] password=[123£]
no colon: error: Basic credentials have no colon
not base64: error: credentials are not a token68
missing padding: error: Basic credentials are not valid base64
padding in the middle: error: credentials are not a token68
space inside: error: credentials are not a token68
url-safe alphabet: error: Basic credentials are not valid base64
invalid UTF-8: error: Basic credentials are not UTF-8
newline in the user: error: the user has a control character
scheme only: error: no credentials after the scheme
scheme and a space: error: no credentials after the scheme
Basicx: another scheme
Bearer: another scheme
empty: another scheme
too long: error: credentials too long
true
-- Bearer parsing
plain: token=[abc.def-ghi_jkl~+/=]
lowercase: token=[T]
padding then more: error: credentials are not a token68
space inside: error: credentials are not a token68
quote: error: credentials are not a token68
no token: error: no credentials after the scheme
no token, space: error: no credentials after the scheme
Basic: another scheme
Bearerx: another scheme
